  "worked_solution": "We differentiate the given function with respect to $x,$ treating all other variables as constants. \n\nFirst, we use the product rule:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}_{x}(x,y) & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy))\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we use the chain and constant multiple rules:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{∂}{∂x}({x}^{3})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+{x}^{3}\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)) & =(3{x}^{2})\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)+{x}^{3}\\cdot (-\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy))\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(xy) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{x}^{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot y\\cdot \\frac{∂}{∂x}(x) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{x}^{3}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\cdot (1) \\\\  & =3{x}^{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(xy)-{x}^{3}y\\operatorname{sin}⁡(xy)\\end{aligned}\n$$",
